WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:07.020
There's lots of things about the world under
Donald Trump that make me despair for humanity

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:12.030
or that make me worried or that shock me or
surprise me or whatever else.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.099
But one of the things that I really just straight
up resent about the Trump administration is

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:22.070
that it's forcing us to have to reexplain
and a lot of really simple concepts that I

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.989
previously thought we sort of had a pretty
firm grasp on that have apparently been thrown

00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:27.659
out the window under Donald Trump.

00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:32.009
So for example, tariffs, I talked yesterday
about tariffs extensively.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:35.530
China and Mexico don't pay for Donald Trump's
tariffs.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.899
The American companies and the American people
who import the stuff from China and Mexico

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:42.579
are the ones actually paying for the tariffs.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:43.579
Voter fraud.

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:45.710
We just talked about it in the first segment
today.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.620
Doesn't matter what Trump and his followers
say in person voter fraud to the t to the

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.739
tune of these three to 5 million illegal votes,
Donald Trump claims took place in 2016 it

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:56.839
doesn't exist.

00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:59.440
Okay, well we've talked about it all.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.149
Brennan Center for Justice Study.

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:05.800
Uh, we, we know it's just, it's just not real
and we're having to reexplain this under Donald

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.800
Trump.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.000
I could go on and give you a long list, but
I want to focus in on one specific one today,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.600
which is that under Trump, since Trump's tax
reform plan was put in place, all of a sudden

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.470
people are pretending that his tax cut would
go to the middle class and that the part that

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:27.500
goes to the rich is also good because it gives,
uh, the economy more juice, so to speak.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.190
There's this idea that giving tax cuts to
the rich stimulates the economy.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.190
It trickles down.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.190
All of that stuff.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:34.240
We've already dealt with this.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.240
Okay.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.240
I've been dealing with it for years.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.240
We've been dealing with it on the program.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.690
Most recently we dealt with it under George
W. Bush.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.080
Tax Cuts for the rich aren't particularly
stimulative to the economy and Republican

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.900
tax plans mostly give disproportionate amounts
of money to the rich and to big corporations

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.500
no matter what they tell you.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.050
And once again, that's what happened with
the Trump republican tax reform that was passed

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.450
during Donald Trump's first term.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:04.550
There's a really great report from the Congressional
Research Service called the economic effects

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.820
of the 2017 tax revision.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.670
Preliminary observations.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.860
You might remember we were told it would be
great for all Americans.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.460
We were told it would let makers keep their
money.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.760
It would incentivize businesses to invest
more in their businesses and in their employees,

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.930
which would cause wages to rise.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.910
It would stimulate economic growth.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.600
We were told that even though in the short
term it would reduce the amount of money that

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.910
the government takes in that it would very
quickly pay for itself because of all the

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.210
growth and winning and all of this that would
be created and ultimately the government would

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.950
actually be taking in more money.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.690
None of it has happened.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.940
Wages have continued to increase slowly, but
they're increasing at the same rate that they

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.050
were increasing before the tax reform plan
went into effect.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:55.640
Growth has continued on the same trend line
as before, the tax reform plan, but what did

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:00.740
happen as a result of Trump's tax plan is
lower the effective tax rate for the super

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:05.480
rich by a significant percentage and hugely
in terms of the raw dollars.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.680
That went back to the very rich relative to
the middle class and the lower middle class

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.700
and the poor.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.560
So Trump personally and his friends made out
really, really well from this tax plan.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:21.870
What it did do was cause businesses to use
the money not to reinvest in their own businesses

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:28.170
or employees, but to start repurchasing shares
of their own stock to drive up the price,

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:34.990
which again is a way of using the money from
the tax cuts to mostly help they're big shareholders

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.370
and their executives.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.840
It's almost like we knew this would happen
when they first started talking about this

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.930
type of tax reform because this is how it
happens every single time.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:49.510
And I want to be really clear, this is not
me speaking out against the tax plan because

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.240
I'm jealous that the tax plan was bad for
me and good for other people.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.220
This tax reform was very good for me.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.220
Okay.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.099
I did a whole segment several months ago when
I had filed my taxes, explaining how, even

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:07.420
though the David Pakman show grew from 2017
to 2018 my effective tax rate as the majority

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:14.140
owner of the David Pakman show went down from
26% effective federal tax rate for the 2017

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:20.370
tax year, 26% down to under 22% in 2018 I'll
take the money.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.370
Okay.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:26.870
But my point in talking about that in talking
about it again here is that it is not economically

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.240
stimulative in terms of policy to do the type
of tax reform.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.430
That saves me like 15% on taxes.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:41.330
Four out of 26 is roughly about 15% and disproportionately
more going to the very, very rich and corporations

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:46.340
who are saving the money, who are using the
money to repurchase a, to do stock buy backs,

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.340
etc.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:52.159
Last thing, we call these the Trump tax cuts,
but really they're republican tax cuts.

00:04:52.159 --> 00:04:56.629
So if you're not happy with the tax reform
plan, yes, Trump is to blame and yes, Trump

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.629
should be voted out.

00:04:57.629 --> 00:04:59.809
In 2020 he supported the tax plan.

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:03.550
He worked on the tax plan with Republicans,
but it's the Republicans who wrote it and

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:07.990
actually pushed it through in the House and
Senate who are also responsible and they should

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:13.180
also be voted out in 2020 really important
not to forget that and blame this all on Trump

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.120
because it is much, much bigger than Donald
Trump.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.120
Let me know what you think.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.479
I'm on Twitter at d pacman.

